{
  "summary": "The bug is caused by double HTML entity escaping. In server/api.go, the `escapeAttr` function converts special characters to HTML entities (e.g., `<` to `&lt;`) when embedding values into data attributes on card elements (data-plan, data-impl-spec, data-test-spec, data-plan-exploration-summary, data-impl-notes). Then in server/templates/client.html, when these values are retrieved via `getAttribute` and displayed, they are passed through the JavaScript `escapeHtml` function which escapes them a second time (e.g., `&lt;` becomes `&amp;lt;`). The fix is to remove the `escapeHtml()` calls around the data attribute values in the item detail rendering code (around lines 923-963 in client.html), since the values are already safely escaped by the server-side `escapeAttr`. The affected sections are: Plan, Plan Exploration Summary, Implementation Spec, Test Spec, and Implementation Notes."
}
